{"t": 674.183, "n": 110, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The self-check is still running in the background, so I have no result yet. I'm not starting a second copy, and I'm not changing any files while it runs.\n\n**Where things stand**\n- Row 2.4 was the only unmarked row. I added `CST-AC5` to the `test_machine_index_and_all_roots` comment and added an assertion that `rows.index_roots(home_path())` still lists the gone root as `missing`. `tests/test_reports.py` passes (16 tests), and the new assertion held on the first run, since it pins existing behaviour.\n- All seven plan rows are marked, and the plan's status is `completed`.\n- I updated `docs/tasks/i144.report.md` with the row 2.4 run and corrected its row count. The earlier report said six rows; the plan has seven.\n- The working tree has three modified files: the plan, the report and `test_reports.py`.\n\nI have not yet seen the result of the final run of the three verification commands: `python -m pytest`, `ruff check src tests` and `mypy`. If it reports a failure, I'll fix it and run it once more. Until then I can't report `tests_passed`, so I'm leaving it as `no`.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: docs/tasks/i144.report.md\nARTIFACT tests_passed: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "884abb9c-3af8-4726-a4ee-1debd137d673"}
